    {
      "section_id": "trainingpromptengineeringaitraining_06_detail_section",
      "section_order": 6,
      "html_id": null,
      "element": "section",
      "section_name": "Detail Section",
      "section_heading": "Good questions.",
      "heading_level": "h2",
      "eyebrow": "A little more clarity",
      "subheading": "",
      "description": "",
      "paragraphs": [
        "A little more clarity",
        "Yes, it's designed for them. No coding is involved anywhere in the session; if your team writes emails, reports, analyses or content, they're the audience. Mixed technical/non-technical batches also work well.",
        "ChatGPT and Gemini as the primary tools, with the techniques taught deliberately transferable to Copilot, Claude and whatever your company adopts next. If you've standardized on one platform, the exercises run on that one.",
        "Our staff shouldn't paste client data into chatbots. That concern is a module, not a footnote: what never goes into a prompt, how to use anonymized stand-ins, and what your company policy should cover. Teams leave more productive AND more careful.",
        "Most teams run it as a 1 or 2 day intensive per batch. It's the fastest track we offer, and the most common first engagement for companies trying us out."
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "A little more clarity"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Good questions."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Is this AI training suitable for non-technical employees?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Yes, it's designed for them. No coding is involved anywhere in the session; if your team writes emails, reports, analyses or content, they're the audience. Mixed technical/non-technical batches also work well."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Which AI tools does the training cover?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "ChatGPT and Gemini as the primary tools, with the techniques taught deliberately transferable to Copilot, Claude and whatever your company adopts next. If you've standardized on one platform, the exercises run on that one."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "What about data security?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Our staff shouldn't paste client data into chatbots. That concern is a module, not a footnote: what never goes into a prompt, how to use anonymized stand-ins, and what your company policy should cover. Teams leave more productive AND more careful."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "How long is the program?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Most teams run it as a 1 or 2 day intensive per batch. It's the fastest track we offer, and the most common first engagement for companies trying us out."
        }
      ],
